          "dossier": {
            "en": "The AA-12 (Auto Assault-12) is an American 12-gauge automatic combat shotgun originally designed by Maxwell Atchisson in 1972 and substantially redesigned by Military Police Systems. It is known for its fully automatic firing capability, distinctive polymer exterior, and large detachable box or drum magazines.Atchisson AA-12 with box magazine",
            "tc": "The AA-12 (Auto Assault-12) is an American 12-gauge automatic combat shotgun originally designed by Maxwell Atchisson in 1972 and substantially redesigned by Military Police Systems. It is known for its fully automatic firing capability, distinctive polymer exterior, and large detachable box or drum magazines.Atchisson AA-12 with box magazine",
            "sc": "The AA-12 (Auto Assault-12) is an American 12-gauge automatic combat shotgun originally designed by Maxwell Atchisson in 1972 and substantially redesigned by Military Police Systems. It is known for its fully automatic firing capability, distinctive polymer exterior, and large detachable box or drum magazines.Atchisson AA-12 with box magazine"
          }
