      "intel": [
        {
          "id": "№1",
          "title": {
            "en": "№1",
            "tc": "№1",
            "sc": "№1"
          },
          "dossier": {
            "en": "* The actual name for this gun is the Smith & Wesson Model 29, a large N-frame, double-action revolver chambered in the devastating .44 Remington Magnum.",
            "tc": "* The actual name for this gun is the Smith & Wesson Model 29, a large N-frame, double-action revolver chambered in the devastating .44 Remington Magnum.",
            "sc": "* The actual name for this gun is the Smith & Wesson Model 29, a large N-frame, double-action revolver chambered in the devastating .44 Remington Magnum."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "№2",
          "title": {
            "en": "№2",
            "tc": "№2",
            "sc": "№2"
          },
          "dossier": {
            "en": "*Introduced in 1955, it was primarily designed for large-game handgun hunting before becoming a cinematic pop-culture legend.",
            "tc": "*Introduced in 1955, it was primarily designed for large-game handgun hunting before becoming a cinematic pop-culture legend.",
            "sc": "*Introduced in 1955, it was primarily designed for large-game handgun hunting before becoming a cinematic pop-culture legend."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "№3",
          "title": {
            "en": "№3",
            "tc": "№3",
            "sc": "№3"
          },
          "dossier": {
            "en": "*The Most Powerful Gun?: In the iconic movie scene, Dirty Harry famously states, \"This is a .44 Magnum, the most powerful handgun in the world...\" While this was true when the Model 29 was launched in 1955, by the time the film was released in 1971, much more powerful cartridges (like the wildcat .454 Casull) already existed.",
            "tc": "*最強大的槍？：在經典電影場景中，髒哈利 (Dirty Harry) 有句名言：「這是一把 .44 Magnum，世界上最強大的手槍……」雖然在 1955 年 Model 29 上市時確實如此，但到了 1971 年電影上映時，威力更大的子彈（如非標準規格的 .454 Casull）早已問世。",
            "sc": "*最强大的枪？：在经典电影场景中，脏哈利 (Dirty Harry) 有句名言：「这是一把 .44 Magnum，世界上最强大的手枪……」虽然在 1955 年 Model 29 上市时确实如此，但到了 1971 年电影上映时，威力更大的子弹（如非标准规格的 .454 Casull）早已问世。"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "№4",
          "title": {
            "en": "№4",
            "tc": "№4",
            "sc": "№4"
          },
          "dossier": {
            "en": "*Frank Sinatra's Gun: The role of Dirty Harry was originally offered to Frank Sinatra. Sinatra actually accepted the role and spent weeks practicing drawing a Model 29, but he ultimately had to drop out of the film after a severe wrist injury made it physically impossible for him to handle the heavy revolver.",
            "tc": "*法蘭克·辛納屈的槍：髒哈利的角色最初是提供給法蘭克·辛納屈的。辛納屈實際上接受了這個角色，並花了幾個星期的時間練習拔出 M29 左輪手槍，但由於嚴重的手腕受傷，導致他無法握持這把沉重的左輪手槍，最終不得不退出這部電影。",
            "sc": "*法兰克·辛纳屈的枪：脏哈利的角色最初是提供给法兰克·辛纳屈的。辛纳屈实际上接受了这个角色，并花了几个星期的时间练习拔出 M29 左轮手枪，但由于严重的手腕受伤，导致他无法握持这把沉重的左轮手枪，最终不得不退出这部电影。"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "№5",
          "title": {
            "en": "№5",
            "tc": "№5",
            "sc": "№5"
          },
          "dossier": {
            "en": "*When ignited inside the heavy steel cylinder, the powder charge generates an immense pressure of up to 36,000 PSI to slam the heavy 240-grain lead bullet down the rifling. The bullet explodes out of the 6.5-inch barrel at a blistering 1,350 to 1,450 feet per second (fps), sending a massive shockwave downrange. Upon impact, it dumps roughly 1,000 to 1,100 foot-pounds of energy, creating a massive wound cavity and driving deep enough to drop a 600-pound grizzly bear in its tracks.",
            "tc": "*When ignited inside the heavy steel cylinder, the powder charge generates an immense pressure of up to 36,000 PSI to slam the heavy 240-grain lead bullet down the rifling. The bullet explodes out of the 6.5-inch barrel at a blistering 1,350 to 1,450 feet per second (fps), sending a massive shockwave downrange. Upon impact, it dumps roughly 1,000 to 1,100 foot-pounds of energy, creating a massive wound cavity and driving deep enough to drop a 600-pound grizzly bear in its tracks.",
            "sc": "*When ignited inside the heavy steel cylinder, the powder charge generates an immense pressure of up to 36,000 PSI to slam the heavy 240-grain lead bullet down the rifling. The bullet explodes out of the 6.5-inch barrel at a blistering 1,350 to 1,450 feet per second (fps), sending a massive shockwave downrange. Upon impact, it dumps roughly 1,000 to 1,100 foot-pounds of energy, creating a massive wound cavity and driving deep enough to drop a 600-pound grizzly bear in its tracks."
          }
        }
      ],
